Sure thing!  A "loop" is a way of repeating a sequence of instructions.  For example, if you wanted to repeat the following statements 5 times:

for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    printf("The number is %d\n", i);
}

You could use a "for loop" to accomplish this:

n = 5;   // set the number of times to repeat the statements

i = 0;   // initialize i to 0

while (i < n) {
    printf("The number is %d\n", i);
    i++;
}

